s4_riso — «Почему Гренландия кажется размером с Африку» (animated risograph / screen-print style test)

Geography
- Coastlines and country borders: Natural Earth 1:50m (public domain), via the npm package world-atlas@2
  (countries-50m.json, ISC licence, Mike Bostock). Africa = dissolved African countries; Greenland = ISO 304.
- Projection maths: d3-geo 3 (ISC licence) for Mercator and spherical areas; topojson-client 3 (ISC) for merging.
- Greenland's move is a rigid rotation of the sphere (its centroid carried to each target, north kept up), then
  re-projected in Mercator every frame, so the shrink is the true Mercator scale change. Area check on this data:
  Africa 29.99 M km², Greenland 2.155 M km², ratio 13.9 (on-screen numbers use the standard 30.4 / 2.17 M km²).
  The 14 "stamps" are Greenland transplanted to the centres of 14 equal-area k-means cells of Africa.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, licence files in fonts/)
- Unbounded (Google Fonts / NARRATIVE), via @fontsource/unbounded
- IBM Plex Mono (IBM), via @fontsource/ibm-plex-mono

Everything else (riso print shader, layout, animation, sound design) is our own code in src/.
Sound: synthesised in numpy (noise + sines), no samples, no music.
